zAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-19T08:05:57Z","updated_at":"2024-11-19T08:05:57Z","body":"If you modify the example as follows, there is no longer a memory leak:\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\nfunc _ready() -> void:\r\n    var a = GDScript.new()\r\n    for i in 100:\r\n        for j in 10:\r\n            a.source_code = \"extends Object\\nvar value = 2212\"\r\n            a.reload()\r\n        await get_tree().create_timer(1).timeout\r\n```\r\n\r\nSo I think this is a duplicate of #77513. The problem is not `reload()`, but that `GDScript` resources are never removed due to extra reference in `GDScriptCache`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2484976974/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2485702189","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99169#issuecomment-2485702189","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/